---
title: 'Build it once. Then type it cold.'
slug: 'build-it-then-type-it-cold'
date: 2026-08-22
excerpt: 'Scripture Builder is the pass that makes a verse stay.'
tags: ['teacher-tip', 'doctrinal-mastery']
author: 'Patrick'
---

Study is first contact. Build is where you understand it — reconstruct the verse from tiles. Then Prove: type it with hints, then type it cold.

That last pass lasts past Friday’s quiz.

Open any of the 100 doctrinal mastery scriptures. Pick one verse. Build it today. Type it cold tomorrow. Daily review keeps it sealed in.

Teachers can assign that two-day pass without writing a new lesson.
